      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The belief that you are fundamentally broken is a heavy burden, but it's also a very powerful, very painful feeling that can be addressed. While the actions you regret are real, they do not define your entire worth as a human being. Even when things feel irreparable, seeking professional support can offer a path toward understanding and change. Please consider talking to a therapist who can help you navigate this self-judgment with compassion.",
      "source": "target",
