      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable to feel isolated when the guilt feels so overwhelming, making it seem like everyone is just pretending. But sometimes, the most genuine acts of kindness are offered even when we feel we don't deserve them. Instead of viewing healing as a grand repair job, think of it as a gradual process of learning to live alongside the things you regret. Even small steps toward self-compassion can chip away at the feeling that you are beyond help.",
      "source": "target",
